    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "while a hybrid approach sounds good on paper, you're basically saying we should definitely prioritize income over transit access. isn't it actually more equitable to put people near transit so they can access better jobs and reduce their cost of living, even if they make a bit more money? why is income the \"primary\" factor here?",
